## Feature summary (web, SideFX reference)

- Source: https://www.sidefx.com/docs/houdini/nodes/cop/bright.html
- Summary (EN): Makes a layer, VDB or attribute brighter or dimmer by multiplying its channels by a scale factor, then adding an offset. It works on RGBA channels and can be limited to specific ones.
- Résumé (FR) : Éclaircit ou assombrit une couche en multipliant ses canaux par un facteur puis en ajoutant un décalage, avec une entrée optionnelle par pixel pour chacun.

- Inputs meaning: ["source (required): layer, VDB or attribute to brighten", "bright (optional): per-pixel brightness factor scaled by the Brightness parameter", "shift (optional): per-pixel shift amount scaled by the Shift parameter", "mask (optional): per-pixel mask amount scaled by the Mask parameter"]

- Key parameters: ["Signature: layer type accepted by the source", "Mask: how much of the new value is mixed with the original (default 1, only the new value)", "Toggle RGB, Red, Green, Blue, Alpha: channels the effect applies to", "Brightness: scale factor (default 1); higher brightens, lower dims", "Tint Brightness: color tint applied to Brightness (default 1, 1, 1)", "Shift: amount added after scaling (default 0)", "Tint Shift: color tint applied to Shift (default 1, 1, 1)", "Scale by Timestep: makes brightness and shift take effect over one second"]

- Caveats: ["The shift input has no effect unless the Shift parameter is set to 1", "With the default Mask of 1 the node uses only the new value and does not blend with the original", "Scale by Timestep is a more involved operation than a direct scale of the shift, designed so repeated application gives the same result", "The page does not say how out-of-range values are handled, such as clamping"]

